  'st-james-retirement-development-residents-oppose-2026-11-22',
  'St James and Kalk Bay residents push back on planned retirement complex',
  'Community', '2026-11-22', 'Cape Town Etc', 'https://www.capetownetc.com/news/kalk-bay-residents-vow-to-fight-proposed-st-james-development/',
  'Locals in St James and Kalk Bay are contesting a proposed retirement development on rail-agency land, while PRASA says the plan is still at an early stage.',
  'A proposal to build an upmarket retirement apartment complex on railway-owned land along the St James coastline is meeting resistance from nearby residents. The land belongs to PRASA, and a development lease for the site has been granted through Intersite, its property subsidiary, Eyewitness News reports. An artist impression shown to residents reportedly depicted a four-storey building.

The local ratepayers and residents association argues that heritage, nature and open access along this stretch of shore should come before commercial interests, and sees the land as a shared public resource. Residents have also raised worries about traffic, emergency access, parking, heritage and the loss of sea views. The association says it will review the original tender process, take part in public participation at every approval stage and has not ruled out legal action. A public meeting on 13 November drew more than 400 people.

PRASA responded on 19 November, saying the proposal is at an early stage and that no statutory applications have been submitted. It says the land is underused and that the development could bring in income to support passenger rail services. The agency says St James Station will stay open and train services will not be affected. The Kromkrans Joint Venture is named as the developer responsible for planning and approvals, including environmental and heritage studies.

Any application will need to go through the formal approval process, and PRASA says stakeholders will be able to submit comments or objections while planning is under way. Residents who want to follow the matter can watch for those public participation notices.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.capetownetc.com/news/kalk-bay-residents-vow-to-fight-proposed-st-james-development/", "https://www.ewn.co.za/2026/11/16/residents-ready-to-fight-proposed-st-james-retirement-development"]',
  'agent'
);
